# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository and in every working tree.
#
# Why this is load-bearing here:
#
#   1. Biome's formatter requires LF, and `npm run lint` is this repo's release
#      gate (there is no CI -- release.sh runs it). On Windows with
#      `core.autocrlf=true`, a fresh clone or worktree checks out CRLF, every
#      source file fails `biome check`, and the release stops before it builds.
#
#   2. release.sh rewrites server.json with jq, which writes CRLF on Windows.
#      Without this file git committed those bytes as-is: server.json carried
#      CRLF in the repository from v0.13.5 until this file renormalized it.
#
#   3. release.sh, bin/lemonsqueezy-mcp.mjs and scripts/*.mjs are executed
#      directly. A CRLF shebang fails on Linux and macOS.
#
# `text=auto` still lets git detect binary content and leave it untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts are always text and always LF, never autodetected.
*.sh text eol=lf
